  "english": "Gospel of John 6:48. \"I am the bread of life.\" to verse 55. \"on the last day.\"\nThird Friday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 95 [96]. \"All the ends [of the earth] have seen.\" Epistle, 2 Timothy 3:1. \"Know this.\" to verse 7. \"never arrive.\" Gospel of John 6:64. \"The spirit is the life-giver.\" to verse 72. \"and he was one of the twelve.\"\nIf here, according to the showing of the calendar, a Fourth Sunday is required, see the second Sunday after Transfiguration; but for the Patristic [Harts] hymn, see the calendar.\n\nAfter the octave, a feast; if they celebrate the feast, these are they:\nFirst: Feast of the Nativity of Saint John the Forerunner. Tone 1 [ahk]: \"Sun [of righteousness]\" (Aregakn), with its proper [canon]. Morning Song: \"You, child.\" Litany: \"God great and powerful.\" Magnificat [Mankunk] Tone 8 [dzk]: \"Supreme of prophets.\" Midday Introit: \"The forerunning.\" Hymn Tone 8 [dzk]: \"Today the church rejoices.\" Psalm: \"You, child, prophet.\" Proverbs 8:4. \"To you, O men, I call.\" to verse 11. \"is not compared to her.\" Prophet Malachi 4:5. \"Thus says the Lord, and behold I.\" to verse 7. \"and justice.\" Prophet Isaiah 40:3. \"The voice of one crying.\" to verse 5. \"the salvation of our God.\" Acts 13:25. \"And as [John] was finishing.\" to verse 33. \"raising up Jesus.\" Alleluia: \"The forerunner John, being terrified.\" Gospel of Luke 1:57. \"And Elisabeth's time was fulfilled.\" to verse 80. \"of his showing to Israel.\"\n\nThen, of the Saints, Peter the Patriarch, Blaise the Bishop, and Abisalom the Deacon. Patristic [Harts] Tone 6 [gdz]: \"Who communed.\" Magnificat [Mankunk] and Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [gd]: \"New youth.\" Midday Introit: \"The patriarchal.\" Hymn Tone 5 [gd]: \"Today the heavenly ones.\" Psalm 131 [132]. \"Your priests.\" Refrain: \"Remember, Lord, David.\" Proverbs (Wisdom of Solomon) 5:1. \"Then shall the righteous stand.\" to verse 8. \"has been of help to us.\" Prophet Jeremiah (Baruch) 3:31. \"There is none that knows.\" to verse 4:4. \"are known to us.\" Epistle, Romans 8:28. \"But we know that to them.\" to verse 39. \"which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.\" Alleluia: \"Priests.\" Gospel of John ... [the text has some corrupt/missing lines in the source transitioning through 1 Timothy] ... so that men might stand. to [1 Timothy] 3:13. \"which is in Christ Jesus.\" Alleluia: of the Fast, from the Tone. Gospel of John 2:12. \"After this Jesus went down.\" to verse 22. \"which Jesus had said.\"\nFirst Friday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 97 [98], antiphon: \"All the ends have seen.\" Refrain: \"O sing.\" Epistle, 1 Timothy 4:1. \"But the Holy Spirit.\" to verse 12. \"let no one despise your youth.\" Alleluia: of the Fast, from the Tone. Gospel of John 2:23. \"And when he was in Jerusalem.\" to verse 3:12. \"will you believe?\"\n\nSecond Sunday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 64 [65], (PZS). \"Praise is due to you.\" Prophet Isaiah 58:13. \"Thus says the Lord to Israel: If you turn.\" to 59:7. \"in their paths.\" Epistle, 1 Timothy 4:12. \"But be an example.\" to 5:10. \"she has followed after.\" Gospel of John 3:13. \"And no one has ascended into heaven.\" to verse 21. \"that they were wrought in God.\"\nSecond Wednesday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 85 [86]. \"Save your servant.\" Epistle, 1 Timothy 5:17. \"Let the elders who rule well.\" to 6:5. \"withdraw yourself from such.\" Gospel of John 3:22. \"After this Jesus came.\" to verse 36. \"remains upon him.\"\nSecond Friday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 97 [98]. \"All the ends have seen.\" Epistle, 2 Timothy 2:3. \"Share in suffering.\" to verse 14. \"to the ruining of the hearers.\" Gospel of John 5:31. \"If I bear witness.\" to verse 47. \"will you believe my words?\"\n\nThird Sunday. Midday Liturgy Psalm [64/65]: \"Praise is due to you.\" Prophet Isaiah 62:1. \"For Zion's sake I will not keep silent.\" to verse 11. \"to the ends of the earth.\" Epistle, 2 Timothy 2:15. \"Study to present yourself.\" to verse 19. \"the name of the Lord.\" Alleluia: of the Resurrection, from the Tone. Gospel of John 6:39. \"This is the will of my Father.\" to verse 47. \"receives eternal life.\"\nThird Wednesday. Midday Liturgy Psalm 85 [86]. \"Save your servant.\" Epistle, 2 Timothy 2:20. \"But in a great house.\" to verse 26. \"to his will.\" Alleluia: of the Fast, from the Tone. Gospel [of John...]",
